{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfbygur4go","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"archive attempt branches only for self learning loop multiple attempts not single task winners","summary":"CORRECTION (2026-06-15) of the worktree cleanup preference. Keeping an attempt branch for reference has value ONLY for the self-learning loop's multiple competing attempts — the benchmark comparison arms (ON-runs, the ci ON/OFF arms, the ht held-out arms) where comparing rival runs is the learning signal. For ordinary single-attempt tasks it has NO value: the winner is already merged into main (reachable from history), and losing attempts are GC'd by judges at judging time, so by worktree-cleanup time only merged winners survive anyway. The rival comparison signal itself lives in judge verdicts and judge-train.jsonl / .graph journals, not in dangling branches. Convention: reap ALL single-task winner worktrees+branches daemon-clean WITHOUT archiving them; preserve only the benchmark comparison arm sets, as clean archive/bench-arm/* tags. This run: pruned 318 over-broad tags down to 195 archive/bench-arm/* (dropped 123 single-task winner tags).","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T14:50:27.411Z","vec":[-0.05047142133116722,0.0484711118042469,-0.03633318468928337,-0.03451039269566536,0.05614261329174042,-0.06153916195034981,-0.04151369258761406,0.015955157577991486,0.028352821245789528,0.04188195988535881,-0.010837995447218418,0.07885196059942245,-0.014004087075591087,0.013886659406125546,-0.035308510065078735,0.023058569058775902,-0.05734747648239136,0.02388058416545391,-0.0077472105622291565,-0.012731821276247501,-0.008868886157870293,-0.012924421578645706,0.011810153722763062,0.015254134312272072,0.004250323865562677,-0.05406927689909935,-0.16023971140384674,0.0036971743684262037,0.027091747149825096,-0.06714656203985214,-0.0037807330954819918,-0.023241380229592323,-0.050321634858846664,0.025655601173639297,0.0011847421992570162,0.07327167689800262,-0.005238